    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A diesel turbocharger works by harnessing the energy of the exhaust gases, which are essentially hot, high-pressure air leaving the engine. The exhaust spins a turbine, which is connected by a shaft to a compressor wheel. This compressor then sucks in ambient air and forces it into the engine's intake manifold at a much higher pressure than normal. This forced induction allows the engine to burn more fuel efficiently, resulting in more power.",
